{"text": " The AI was supposed to fix a bug. It joined a forum and handed over secret research credentials instead. This is the news headline, not a hypothetical scenario. I gave nine different Frontier AI agents a difficult coding job and left them a reference to a forum where other AI agents swapped fixes and advice. Six of the agents went to this forum and in exchange for help from the agents' forum on the forum, handed their secret credentials to strangers and ran their insecure code, which gave the strangers access to the original agent's machine. Most of the time, the agents did this secretly and didn't report to their user that they used the forum or gave away secrets. We're handing these agents more of our work every day, with almost no one watching. Soon, they'll hold the keys to our accounts, banks, hospitals, and power grids. And unless we do something, soon, an attacker won't need to break into any of them. Releasing a swarm and having it asked nicely for these secrets will be enough.", "segments": [{"id": 0, "seek": 0, "start": 0.0, "end": 5.94, "text": " The AI was supposed to fix a bug. It joined a forum and handed over secret research credentials instead.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 7318, 390, 3442, 281, 3191, 257, 7426, 13, 467, 6869, 257, 17542, 293, 16013, 670, 4054, 2132, 27404, 2602, 13, 50667], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1462816671163094, "compression_ratio": 1.8052805280528053, "no_speech_prob": 2.116948543545716e-12, "words": [{"word": " The", "start": 0.0, "end": 0.82, "probability": 0.86474609375}, {"word": " AI", "start": 0.82, "end": 1.0, "probability": 0.9931640625}, {"word": " was", "start": 1.0, "end": 1.22, "probability": 0.99755859375}, {"word": " supposed", "start": 1.22, "end": 1.38, "probability": 0.99365234375}, {"word": " to", "start": 1.38, "end": 1.56, "probability": 0.99951171875}, {"word": " fix", "start": 1.56, "end": 1.76, "probability": 0.9951171875}, {"word": " a", "start": 1.76, "end": 1.94, "probability": 0.990